From 3a4090e62238927575cd7b8e352c9f5eed2777f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 18:48:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Rebuild speaking scoring on the official 4-part rubric
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replace the inferred five-criteria B2 sheet (content/speakingCriteria.js)
with the school's actual method, supplied directly: one holistic band per
part (Part 1.1, 1.2, 2, 3 — maxes 5/5/5/6), each on its own CEFR-labelled
scale, verbatim in content/speakingRubric.js.

- New raw-to-reported conversion table (0-21 -> 0-75) in ScoreConversion.js,
  replacing the old 0-36 weighted-criteria table this used to run on; plain
  sum, no weighting, mirroring how writing is already scored.
- New services/SpeakingScoring.js (mirrors WritingScoring.js): plain-sum
  expert mark, official conversion, and a partial-submission cap so a
  one-part practice attempt is never scaled up as if it were a whole mock.
- AIEvaluationService's whole-performance prompt rewritten to ask for one
  band per part against the new scales, instead of five criteria bands
  averaged across everything the candidate said.
- ExamResult.criterionBands renamed to partBands (part-keyed, not
  criterion-keyed); teacherBands calibration correction updated to match.
- routes/exam.js and routes/admin.js updated for the new part shape;
  result-screen criteria panel and teacher correction form in app.js
  updated for per-part descriptors (now arrays of bullets) and per-part maxes.
- test/speaking-scoring.test.js covers the conversion table, the partial cap,
  and the rubric's descriptors/next-band lookups.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LgKXYQSxMY9AyY5uyuhSbh
